// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 13 (Impl-R): the wave-body operations
// outside a wave body — the typed surface's scope rule (W2B §3).
// contrib(c,u) stages a payload into the ENCLOSING wave's J(W); with
// no enclosing wave there is nothing to join. read_W reads the
// ENCLOSING wave's frozen capture; with no enclosing wave there is
// no frozen κ. Outside waves the fallback tier's own ops apply
// (lcell_inflate / lcell_merge — the S1 path; lcell_value — read_S:
// defined + session-monotone, schedule-dependent — the mode is in
// the type). MUST FAIL TO COMPILE.

ptr c = lcell_new(1)

fn main() {
    contrib(c, 1, 0)     // no enclosing wave: nothing to join
    int v = read_W(c)    // no enclosing wave: no frozen capture
    print(v)
}
